nio: exec launchd as initproc, not kernproc

Run 613 finally reached exec: load_init_program_at_path /sbin/launchd,
but bsdinit_task() runs on the boot thread, where current_proc() is
kernproc and current_task() is kernel_task.  load_init_program(p) then
execs with p = kernproc; the failed exec's cleanup halts kernel_task and
trips task.c:3126 assert(task != kernel_task), with a kernel-address far.

XNU reaches bsdinit_task() on the init thread, where p is already pid 1.
Do the same here by targeting proc_find(1) for the exec and the process
name, so the failure path halts the init task, not the kernel task.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
--- a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
@@ -1260,6 +1260,6 @@ bsdinit_task(void)
 {
 	nio_bmark("\nnio: BT enter");
-	proc_t p = current_proc();
+	proc_t p = proc_find(1);  /* nio: exec initproc, not kernproc (614) */
 
 	process_name("init", p);
 
